---------------\n[2511.16108v1] SkyRL-Agent: Efficient RL Training for Multi-turn LLM Agent (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.16108v1)\nciteturn2481view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.16108v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 158\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 20 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:SkyRL-Agent: Efficient RL Training for Multi-turn LLM Agent\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Shiyi Cao , cite6†Dacheng Li , cite7†Fangzhou Zhao , cite8†Shuo Yuan , cite9†Sumanth R. Hegde , cite10†Connor Chen , cite11†Charlie Ruan , cite12†Tyler Griggs , cite13†Shu Liu , cite14†Eric Tang , cite15†Richard Liaw , cite16†Philipp Moritz , cite17†Matei Zaharia , cite18†Joseph E. Gonzalez , cite19†Ion Stoica L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled SkyRL-Agent: Efficient RL Training for Multi-turn LLM Agent, by Shiyi Cao and 14 other authors\nL14: cite20†View PDF cite21†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:We introduce SkyRL-Agent, a framework for efficient, multi-turn, long-horizon agent training and evaluation. It provides efficient asynchronous dispatching, lightweight tool integration, and flexible backend interoperability, enabling seamless use with existing RL frameworks such as SkyRL-train, VeRL, and Tinker.\nL16: > Using SkyRL-Agent, we train SA-SWE-32B, a software engineering agent trained from Qwen3-32B (24.4% Pass@1) purely with reinforcement learning. We introduce two key components: an optimized asynchronous pipeline dispatcher that achieves a 1.55x speedup over naive asynchronous batching, and a tool-enhanced training recipe leveraging an AST-based search tool to facilitate code navigation, boost rollout Pass@K, and improve training efficiency.\nL17: Together, these optimizations enable SA-SWE-32B to reach 39.4% Pass@1 on SWE-Bench Verified with more than 2x cost reduction compared to prior models reaching similar performance. Despite being trained solely on SWE tasks, SA-SWE-32B generalizes effectively to other agentic tasks, including Terminal-Bench, BrowseComp-Plus, and WebArena. We further demonstrate SkyRL-Agent's extensibility through case studies on deep research, computer use, and memory agents, each trained using a different training backend.\nL18: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite22†arXiv:2511.16108 [cs.AI]\nL20:    | (or cite23†arXiv:2511.16108v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL21:    | cite24†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.16108†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Shiyi Cao [cite25†view email ]\nL25: [v1] Thu, 20 Nov 2025 07:05:19 UTC (467 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled SkyRL-Agent: Efficient RL Training for Multi-turn LLM Agent, by Shiyi Cao and 14 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * cite20†View PDF L34:   * cite21†HTML (experimental) L35:   * cite26†TeX Source L36: \nL37: cite27†view license L38: \nL39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.AI\nL42: \nL43: cite28†< prev |   cite29†next > L44: \nL45: cite30†new | cite31†recent | cite32†2025-11 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite33†cs L50: ### References & Citations\nL51: \nL52:   * cite34†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L53:   * cite35†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L54:   * cite36†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L55: \nL56: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL57: \nL58: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL59: \nL60: [Button: ×]\nL61: \nL62: loading...\nL63: \nL64: Data provided by:\nL65: \nL66: ### Bookmark\nL67: \nL68: [In